For a given ${\boldsymbol \Psi}=\left\{\psi_1,\cdots,\psi_r\right\}\subseteq L_2({\mathbb R}^d)$ with $d\in{\mathbb N}$, a quasi-affine system ${\mathscr X}({\boldsymbol \Psi})$ generated by ${\boldsymbol \Psi}$ is the collection of the dilations and the shifts of the elements in ${\boldsymbol \Psi}$:
\begin{align} {\mathscr X}({\boldsymbol \Psi})=\left\{\psi_{\alpha,n,{\boldsymbol k}}:1\leq\alpha\leq r,~n\in{\mathbb Z},~{\boldsymbol k}\in{\mathbb Z}^d\right\},
\end{align}
where $\psi_{\alpha,n,{\boldsymbol k}}$ is defined as
\begin{align} \psi_{\alpha,n,{\boldsymbol k}}=\left\{\begin{array}{cl}
2^{\frac{nd}{2}}\psi_{\alpha}(2^n\cdot-{\boldsymbol k})~~&~~n\geq 0;\vspace{0.125em}\\
2^{nd}\psi_{\alpha}(2^n\cdot-2^{n}{\boldsymbol k})~~&~~n<0.
